<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<!--
  Icon of `.orion` documents.

  # Why this fragment exists

  Tauri does declare the association (`bundle.fileAssociations`), but its WiX
  template writes an *advertised* ProgID with no icon: Windows then falls back
  to the executable's own, and a profile is shown to the user with the icon of
  the application that opens it. Nothing in Tauri's configuration distinguishes
  the two — `FileAssociation` has no icon field. A WiX fragment is the only
  hook that avoids vendoring the whole of `main.wxs`, whose drift against the
  CLI version would cost far more than these twenty lines.

  # What it writes

  Two values under the ProgID the template creates, `Orion.orion` — hence the
  coupling: `productName` and the declared extension form that identifier, and
  the `windows_bundle_gives_orion_profiles_their_own_icon` test fails if either
  changes without this key following.

  The icon ships as a resource (`tauri.windows.conf.json`), and is therefore
  installed next to `orion.exe`. Declaring it as a file of this fragment would
  instead look for it from candle's working directory, which is the WiX build
  directory and not the project's.

  # Limite connue

  MSI only. The NSIS package (`cargo xtask orion-msi`, NSIS bundle asked for)
  writes its own association, executable icon included; the MSI is the shipped
  format.

  Note the flag is not spelled out here: two hyphens in a row close nothing in
  XML, they make the comment ill-formed, and candle then rejects the file
  before reading a single element.
-->

<?if $(sys.BUILDARCH)="x86"?>
    <?define Win64 = "no" ?>
<?else?>
    <?define Win64 = "yes" ?>
<?endif?>

<Wix xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/wi">
    <Fragment>
        <DirectoryRef Id="INSTALLDIR">
            <Component Id="OrionProfileIcon" Guid="6175B0FC-02FE-426C-9303-085D7C76784B" Win64="$(var.Win64)">
                <RegistryKey Root="HKLM" Key="Software\Classes\Orion.orion">
                    <!-- Explorer's «Type» column. The advertised ProgID's
                         description already fills it; this one wins, and stays
                         readable while the advertisement is unresolved. -->
                    <RegistryValue Type="string" Name="FriendlyTypeName" Value="Profil de connexion Orion" KeyPath="yes" />
                    <RegistryKey Key="DefaultIcon">
                        <RegistryValue Type="string" Value="&quot;[INSTALLDIR]orion-profile.ico&quot;,0" />
                    </RegistryKey>
                </RegistryKey>
            </Component>
        </DirectoryRef>
    </Fragment>
</Wix>
